1790666150.004	## The Dawn of Mass Communication: A History of the Printing Press
1790666150.004	
1790666150.004	The invention and evolution of the printing press is not merely a technological footnote in human history; it is, arguably, one of the most profound inflection points upon which modern civilization has been built. By radically democratizing knowledge, accelerating scientific discourse, fueling social revolutions, and permanently reshaping religious practice, the printing press became the engine of modernity. Before its advent, knowledge was painstakingly curated by scribes within cloistered institutions; after its proliferation, it exploded outward into a decentralized torrent that irrevocably altered the relationship between humanity and information. Tracing the history of this device is to trace the trajectory of intellectual freedom itself—a journey from painstaking craftsmanship to instantaneous global connectivity.
1790666150.004	
